HST Office: HST PDF's two toolbar rows have the same width and their group separators line up.

Owner request 14/11/2026: the two rows of controls beside the banner were uneven (row 1 ended about 115 px
before row 2) and the group separators did not line up. The controls now stand in one grid: both rows share
the group columns (file | page, zoom | search, edit | sign), the separators run across both rows, the menu
button is centred across both rows, and in each column the shorter row's widest control (page number, search)
takes the rest of the column, so both rows end at the separators. Sign, a custom-painted button that would repeat
its image when stretched, is painted as wide as Edit above it. The block stays centred vertically beside the
banner.

--- a/xmlsecurity/source/hstpdf/pdfviewerwindow.cxx
+++ b/xmlsecurity/source/hstpdf/pdfviewerwindow.cxx
@@ -115,6 +115,15 @@
     rButton.set_accessible_name(aText);
 }
 
+/// Width of the Sign button's image that makes the button as wide as Edit above it in the toolbar grid
+/// (the button's own padding aside), so both toolbar rows end together.
+tools::Long signImageWidth(weld::Widget& rEdit, weld::Widget& rSign)
+{
+    const tools::Long nPadding
+        = std::max<tools::Long>(0, rSign.get_preferred_size().Width() - rSign.get_size_request().Width());
+    return rEdit.get_preferred_size().Width() - nPadding;
+}
+
